== Lexicon ==
Kott had been influenced by [[Turkic languages]], and had borrowed some words from Turkic languages. For example Kott {{Lang|zko|baktîr-}} ‘to praise’ comes from [[Proto-Turkic]] *paktïr (based on phonetics, likely loaned from [[Kumandin language|Kumandin]] or [[Shor language|Shor]]), or Kott {{Lang|zko|kolá}} ‘copper, brass’ comes from Proto-Turkic *kola (of which the source is not phonetically identifiable).<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Khabtagaeva |first=Bayarma |date=2015 |title=Some Remarks on Turkic Elements of Mongolic Origin in Yeniseian |journal=Studia Etymologica Cracoviensia |language=en |volume=20 |issue=2 |pages=111–126 |doi=10.4467/20843836SE.15.008.2794 |doi-access=free}}</ref> At the time of its extinction, it was also loaning words from Russian.

